    "q-81237": {
      "dom_id": "step-q81237",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "If $T=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 9 & -8 & 10 \\\\ -3 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]$ is the standard matrix of the linear transformation $T$, then $\\text{rank}(T)=$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that $\\text{rank}(T)=\\text{dim}(\\text{Im}(T))=\\text{rank}(T).$ \n\nSo, we need to find the rank of the matrix $T.$ We reduce $T$ to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 9 & -8 & 10 \\\\ -3 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, since $T$ has $3$ pivot column, we have that \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(T)=\\text{rank}(T)=3.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
