    "q-81239": {
      "dom_id": "step-q81239",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Given the transformation $T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}2y+z \\\\ -y+5x \\\\ -5x+y\\end{aligned}],$ find its rank.",
      "worked_solution": "First, the standard matrix of $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRecall that $\\text{rank}(T)=\\text{dim}(\\text{Im}(T))=\\text{rank}(T).$ \n\nSo, we need to find the rank of the matrix $T.$ We reduce $T$ to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, since $T$ has $2$ pivot columns, we have that \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(T)=\\text{rank}(T)=2.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
